\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{Forecast accuracy at the 16:00 bar (15:30--16:00). Every forecast is the plain back-transform $f^2B$ ($f$ the forecast on the adjusted scale $\sqrt  {RV/B}$, $B$ the diurnal baseline). QLIKE: against the actual (unwinsorized) realized variance; QLIKE, trimmed: the same forecast against the winsorized training target (diagnostic). \% vs R: the mean daily loss difference against the reference R; DM: Diebold--Mariano statistic on that difference, Newey--West variance (Bartlett, lag 6) with the Harvey--Leybourne--Newbold correction; $\overline  {RV}/\overline  {F}$: mean realized variance over mean forecast; extreme: plain forecasts below PLAIN\_FLOOR on every 16:00 session of the arm span. Point estimates. R = reference, H = recommended headline, $=$ identical to another row.}}{9}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:master_close_accuracy}{{6}{9}{Forecast accuracy at the 16:00 bar (15:30--16:00). Every forecast is the plain back-transform $f^2B$ ($f$ the forecast on the adjusted scale $\sqrt {RV/B}$, $B$ the diurnal baseline). QLIKE: against the actual (unwinsorized) realized variance; QLIKE, trimmed: the same forecast against the winsorized training target (diagnostic). \% vs R: the mean daily loss difference against the reference R; DM: Diebold--Mariano statistic on that difference, Newey--West variance (Bartlett, lag 6) with the Harvey--Leybourne--Newbold correction; $\overline {RV}/\overline {F}$: mean realized variance over mean forecast; extreme: plain forecasts below PLAIN\_FLOOR on every 16:00 session of the arm span. Point estimates. R = reference, H = recommended headline, $=$ identical to another row}{table.6}{}}
