\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{The last-30-min trade: $\mathrm  {sign}(s)$ on the straddle (nearest out-of-the-money call and put, same-day expiry, one position), entered at 15:30, held to the close; buy when the plain 16:00 forecast $f^2B$ exceeds the 15:30 implied variance, sell otherwise. Returns per unit of premium; Sharpe annualized by $\sqrt  {252}$ per trade day; $^{\times }$: the entry pays the spread (buy at the ask, sell at the bid); hit: share of days with a positive midpoint return; buys: days the rule buys. $\Delta $Sharpe: the row minus the reference R (or minus always short) on the same days, point estimates; $t$ vs R: Newey--West HAC $t$ statistic of the mean daily midpoint-return difference against R.}}{13}{table.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:master_close_trade}{{7}{13}{The last-30-min trade: $\mathrm {sign}(s)$ on the straddle (nearest out-of-the-money call and put, same-day expiry, one position), entered at 15:30, held to the close; buy when the plain 16:00 forecast $f^2B$ exceeds the 15:30 implied variance, sell otherwise. Returns per unit of premium; Sharpe annualized by $\sqrt {252}$ per trade day; $^{\times }$: the entry pays the spread (buy at the ask, sell at the bid); hit: share of days with a positive midpoint return; buys: days the rule buys. $\Delta $Sharpe: the row minus the reference R (or minus always short) on the same days, point estimates; $t$ vs R: Newey--West HAC $t$ statistic of the mean daily midpoint-return difference against R}{table.7}{}}
